==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Endless}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|endeles}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|endelēas||endless}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*andijalausaz||endless}}, equivalent to {{suffix|end|less|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|En-us-endless.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# Having no [[end]].
#: '''''endless''' time; '''endless''' praise''
# Extending [[indefinite]]ly.
#: ''an '''endless''' line''
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Without profitable end; fruitless; unsatisfying.
#* Beaumont and Fletcher
#*: All loves are '''endless'''.

